    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "Dimitri devotes $\\frac{1}{3}$ of the day to schoolwork and he spends $\\frac{1}{10}$ of the day watching television. As a fraction of the day, how much more time is spent on schoolwork than on television?",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\frac{7}{30}$ of the day",
      "worked": "The LCM of 3 and 10 is 30.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{10}&=\\frac{10}{30}-\\frac{3}{30}\\\\\\frac{1}{3}-\\frac{1}{10}&=\\frac{7}{30}\\end{align*}$$\n\nDimitri spends $\\frac{7}{30}$ of the day more on schoolwork than on television.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
